Published hyperparameter admission (internal/model/v41_gguf_topology.go)
Upstream paths:
  deepinfer/hugging_face/config.py lines 164-174, 282, 294-298
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/hc_blocks.py lines 84-95
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/moe.py lines 55-60
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/mlp.py lines 164-165
Adaptation: contract-only. DeepInfer reads hc_mult, hc_eps,
hc_sinkhorn_iters, swiglu_limit and norm_topk_prob as required config keys
and asserts norm_topk_prob. Fak turns that required-key admission into
fail-closed published-value admission on the GGUF path: a file whose decoder
schedule is the published V4.1-Flash one must declare HC mult 4, 20 Sinkhorn
iterations, epsilon 1e-6 (compared in float32), SwiGLU clamp 10 and top-k
renormalisation, or it is refused instead of running with forward defaults.
An explicit expert_weights_norm that is false or not a bool is refused on
every deepseek41 GGUF, mirroring the upstream assert on norm_topk_prob.

Shared-layer topology refinement (internal/model/v41_topology_validate.go)
Upstream paths:
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/cross_layer.py lines 181-197
  deepinfer/hugging_face/config.py lines 62-85
Adaptation: Go source-list form of the segmented layer maps. The
index-topk, index-K and KV refinement chain collapses to one check,
kvOwner(indexSource(l)) == kvOwner(l), because fak's index keys are owned by
the KV sources; a layer with no preceding KV source owns itself, as in the
upstream self-reference padding. Unlike upstream, ratio-0 layers and ratio-0
sources are inactive, out-of-range sources are tolerated, a schedule with no
KV source is not checked, and candidate, YOCO, segment and use_swa/index_topk
rules are not ported. The check runs only for non-published GGUF schedules.

Engram table derivation (internal/model/v41_engram_derive.go)
Upstream paths:
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/engram_metadata.py lines 24-27, 78-95, 108-114
  deepinfer/model_executor/models/v4_modules/engram.py lines 42, 53
  deepinfer/hugging_face/config.py lines 195-213
  deepinfer/environ.py line 146
Adaptation: Go port of the table-size prime derivation (next prime from
vocab-1 per ngram table, one seen set across all layers and heads, flattened
[ngram][head]) with deterministic trial division, plus the compressed pad
binding token_map[2] and the odd multiplier generation range from the
NumPy bound. Neither GGUF dialect carries the Engram table vocabulary, so the
check assumes the published 16000000 and runs only for the published
V4.1-Flash Engram geometry (layers 1 and 14, max n-gram 4, 8 heads) when the
serving loader attaches the Engram stage.
